{
  "title": "test_convention_exports is slow (~90s) — dominates make check",
  "description": "The `test_convention_exports.py` test suite validates every exported game file against the JSON schema and takes ~90s, dominating the `make test` target (and therefore `make check`).\n\nBreakdown from `pytest --durations=30`:\n- `test_game_conforms_to_schema` parametrizes over all game exports. The slowest single game takes 11s, top 30 tests account for ~80s total.\n- `test_game_models_exist` takes 11s on its own.\n- Schema validation with jsonschema is the bottleneck — each game file is validated independently.\n\nPossible optimizations:\n- Compile the JSON schema validator once (via `jsonschema.validators.validator_for`) and reuse across parametrized tests. Check if `all_games_data` fixture already caches loading.\n- Only validate game files that changed on the branch (similar to how `make check` now skips targets based on changed files). The conftest already has `changed_files_since_master` — could use it to filter parametrization.\n- Consider a faster JSON schema validator like `fastjsonschema` which compiles schemas to Python code.\n- Profile whether the bottleneck is loading/decompressing game files or the actual schema validation.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "performance",
    "testing",
  ],
